Job Description 
 Build the future with us 
 Do you enjoy turning data into practical solutions that transform the way people work? Join the Strategy and Analytics team within the Underwriting, New Business and Claims Vice-Presidency, where advanced analytics and artificial intelligence are used to optimize underwriting and claims processes in individual insurance.
 As a Data Scientist, you will contribute to end-to-end innovation projects, from exploring new data sources to monitoring the performance of models in production. You will have the opportunity to prototype solutions, propose new approaches, and see the tangible impact of your work on operations and risk management.
 You will contribute to the development of statistical and machine learning models, generative AI prototypes, and automation solutions designed to optimize business processes.
 This position is a great opportunity to showcase your skills and fully realize your potential within a caring and trustworthy company. Here, people and their development are at the heart of our priorities, fostering an environment where collaboration and innovation can thrive.
 What you will accomplish with us 
 As a Data Scientist, you will be at the heart of our mission. Here are your main responsibilities:
 Work closely with business experts to understand their needs, design, test, and explain tailored solutions, and ensure they meet business requirements;
 Explore and analyze structured and unstructured data to generate actionable insights and identify opportunities for modelling, automation, or the use of artificial intelligence;
 Contribute to the end-to-end development of models and AI solutions, from proof of concept to deployment, including data preparation, modelling or prototyping, results evaluation, and documentation;
 Collaborate with project, IT, and data teams to facilitate the integration and production deployment of developed solutions;
 Monitor the performance of solutions and models in production, identify data or model drift, and recommend improvements to optimize performance;
 Incorporate sound risk management practices into the development and evolution of solutions, particularly with respect to privacy, model risk, and responsible AI use;
 Contribute to the adoption of artificial intelligence by sharing your knowledge and identifying opportunities to leverage AI to improve ways of working.
 What could accelerate your success in this role 
 We are looking for someone who:
 Has 2 to 6 years of experience in data science and a university degree in mathematics, statistics, computer science, or another relevant scientific field;
 Has knowledge of the insurance or financial services industry, an asset;
 Is proficient in Python and SQL, as well as various statistical and machine learning techniques;
 Has experience with Databricks, Azure Machine Learning, and Git;
 Has knowledge of Power Platform, an asset;
 Has experience developing solutions that incorporate generative AI or natural language processing, an asset;
 Takes a rigorous, business-focused approach to solving complex problems;
 Communicates effectively and is able to explain complex concepts clearly to different audiences;
 Demonstrates curiosity, autonomy, collaboration, and adaptability.
 Why you will love working with us 
 A work environment where learning and development come together with a shared pursuit of excellence;
 Artificial intelligence is in everyone’s hands, helping you increase your personal effectiveness while supporting the organization’s growth;
 A healthy, safe, equitable, and inclusive environment where everyone’s potential can thrive and develop;
 The opportunity to work in a hybrid environment supported by flexibility and access to inspiring and innovative workspaces.
 Competitive benefits 
 Flexible group insurance;
 Competitive pension plan;
 Employee share purchase plan;
 Vacation, well-being, and personal development days;
 Telemedicine;
 Employee and family assistance program;
 Ergonomic office furniture program;
 Performance bonus;
 Discounts on iA products;
 And much more!
 Apply now and take the lead in your career, where your talent truly matters! 
 Hesitating to apply? 
 At iA, we believe in potential and value diverse experiences. If this role inspires you, take the leap and apply. There may be a place for you with us, and we want to get to know you!
 Location(s) 
Quebec / 1080, Grande Allee West 
